     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     Device manifest (DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE).

     Almost everything the vendor image declares arrives as one of the 104
     fragments under /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/, which are shipped as blobs.
     What is left is the per-SoC part: the stock image carries
     manifest_kera.xml, manifest_sun.xml and manifest_tuna.xml side by side
     because Lenovo builds one vendor image for several SKUs. This device is
     TunaP (soc_id 694), so the contents below are manifest_tuna.xml — which
     declares exactly one HAL that the fragments do not.
-->
<manifest version="8.0" type="device" target-level="202404">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.gatekeeper</name>
        <fqname>IGatekeeper/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
